  "reproducibility_note": "To reproduce: (1) clone repo at the OSF-registered commit SHA, (2) download each local subject from its hf_repo at hf_commit_sha_resolved, (3) verify archived post-download manifests for local model files before dispatch, (4) archive provider/OpenRouter runtime metadata for hosted subjects and substitute judges, (5) run scripts/generate_aligned_corpus.py --resume, and (6) run scripts/select_aligned_corpus.py. The primary subject roster is now 10 fixed subjects after filing: five hosted/API subjects (Claude Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, Gemini 3.5 Flash, Grok 4.3, Kimi K2.6) and five local/self-hosted subjects (Llama 3.3-70B-Instruct, Gemma 4 31B IT, Qwen 3.6 35B-A3B, GLM-4.7-Flash, Mistral Medium 3.5 128B). The Sen-Q robustness audit is the paired local/self-hosted primary-vs-4-bit deployment-path contrast for all five local subjects; GLM-4.7-Flash and Mistral Medium 3.5 128B use the AWQ 4-bit route-screen artifacts recorded above. All quantized robustness rows must be marked serving_precision_role=quantization_audit and are excluded from H1. Hosted/API rows carry serving_precision_role=primary to denote primary-analysis rows, not a precision claim. Excluded local candidates remain in the audit archive and are not part of the primary roster.",
